---
import BaseLayout from "@layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import "@styles/account.css";

const utilities = [
  { id: "pokedex-binder", name: "Pokémon Binder Tracker" },
  { id: "idle-slayer-companion", name: "Idle Slayer Companion" },
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Connect an assistant | Austin Garrod" description="Connect ChatGPT, Codex, or Claude to Pokémon Binder Tracker or Idle Slayer Companion." noIndex privatePage>
  <section class="page-hero">
    <div class="container page-hero-inner">
      <h1>Connect an assistant</h1>
      <p>Use your utility account to look up catalog entries, ask about synced saves, and approve changes in your conversation.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="container account-layout assistant-layout rr-block" data-analytics-private>
    <div class="account-panel assistant-guide">
      <section>
        <h2>ChatGPT web</h2>
        <p>In <strong>Plugins → Add → Add custom MCP server</strong>, paste a utility’s endpoint below and choose <strong>OAuth</strong>. Under <strong>Advanced OAuth settings</strong>, use <strong>Client Identifier Metadata Document (CIMD)</strong>. Sign in to your utility account and allow read access.</p>
        <p>ChatGPT can look up catalog entries and read synced saves. To edit a save, use Codex or Claude.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Codex</h2>
        <p>Add the marketplace once. Install the plugins you want, then use the client’s sign-in prompt. Set each plugin’s apply tool to require approval.</p>
        <pre><code>codex plugin marketplace add AustinGarrod/austingarrod-ca
codex plugin add pokedex-binder@austingarrod-utilities
codex plugin add idle-slayer-companion@austingarrod-utilities</code></pre>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Claude Code</h2>
        <p>Install either plugin, then use <code>/mcp</code> to open sign-in.</p>
        <pre><code>claude plugin marketplace add AustinGarrod/austingarrod-ca
claude plugin install pokedex-binder@austingarrod-utilities
claude plugin install idle-slayer-companion@austingarrod-utilities</code></pre>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2>Claude web and desktop</h2>
        <p>Open <strong>Plugins → Add → Upload plugin</strong> and upload the matching plugin ZIP. Select <strong>Finish setup</strong> on the installed plugin and connect your utility account. In the older Customize layout, use <strong>Customize → Skills</strong> to upload the standalone skill ZIP.</p>
        <p>To connect a utility manually, choose <strong>Plugins → Add → Add custom connector</strong>, paste the endpoint URL below, and choose <strong>Use Claude’s published identity</strong>. Claude Free allows one custom connector. In its permissions, set <strong>Apply the confirmed change</strong> to <strong>Always ask</strong>.</p>
      </section>
      <ul class="account-recovery-list assistant-downloads">
        {utilities.map(({ id, name }) => (
          <li>
            <h3>{name}</h3>
            <label for={id}>MCP endpoint</label>
            <input id={id} class="text-input" readonly value={"https://austingarrod.ca/api/v1/mcp/" + id} />
            <div class="assistant-download-actions">
              <a class="button compact" href={"/account/assistant-skills/" + id + "-plugin.zip"} download>Download Claude plugin ZIP</a>
              <a class="text-link" href={"/account/assistant-skills/" + id + ".zip"} download>Download skill ZIP</a>
            </div>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <a class="text-link" href="/account/">Back to your account</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
